      },
      "text": "**The tournament** (torneamentum) emerged in 11th-century France as organized military exercise that had developed into public spectacle. Geoffrey de Preuilly (died 1066) is credited in Orderic Vitalis with establishing tournament rules, though the exact timing and extent of his contribution is disputed."
    },
